# prose-audit: Grade B — Izabela Sajbor's death is now written at the scale it deserves — Pszczyna, the sister's published messages, and the exact reason waiting was the safe option for every obstetrician in the country — and the march no longer reads its own counters back to the player. The winter-frontier sub-event is still a one-line premise.
