= Security is not a photograph

The confrontation peaks while humanitarian access remains contested.

**September doctrine:** [+ border_doctrine +].

[? if border_doctrine = "Controlled processing with monitored access": The
administrative proposal now needs a winter operating partner, not another
launch.?]
[? if border_doctrine = "Rights-first humanitarian access": Rights groups
expect the Left to protect access when the images become politically costly.?]
[? if border_doctrine = "Security first with deferred scrutiny": The promised
scrutiny has reached its due date.?]
[? if border_doctrine = "Defer to KO": KO still has the microphone; border
towns and humanitarian teams still do not have a Left procedure.?]

- @nov21_corridor
- @nov21_uniforms
- @nov21_observers

@nov21_corridor
title: Propose an EU-backed processing and humanitarian corridor
on-arrival: border_doctrine = "EU-backed processing corridor"; border_security_confidence += 3; minority_safety += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; p2050_relation += 2; pis_relation -= 3; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 9; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6; public_mood_pending_border_security_support -= 3; news_headline = "The Left asks Europe to share border administration"

The proposal reframes the border as an administrative burden to be shared, not
an exception zone outside law. Opponents call it weakness; municipalities call
it the first executable map.

