= Competing ideas of independence

The eleventh of November arrives with the frontier in every speech. The march
organisers have spent the autumn discovering that the Belarus crisis lets them
talk about the nation and the border in the same sentence, and they intend to
do it in front of a hundred thousand people.

[? if civic_independence_years > 0: Our own commemoration has organisers who
expect to be asked again. They have a date in the diary, a list of speakers and
a growing conviction that this is now an annual obligation rather than a
gesture.?]
[? if independence_monitor_years > 0: The observers have kept their files, their
lawyers and their hotline. They will assume the operation is running unless
somebody tells them otherwise.?]
[? if independence_counter_years > 0: The counter-mobilisation contacts are
still live, and the people on them do not need much persuading.?]
[? if independence_join_years > 0: The social-patriotic current has marched
inside the main procession before and treats the contacts it made there as its
own — not the coalition's, and not available to be disowned by a leadership
that authorised them.?]

